---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import thisCannotContinue from "../assets/uni_the_cat_aka_big_boobs.jpg";
import AccordionItem from "../components/custom-ui/accordion/AccordionItem.astro";
import { JorseSpawnerButton } from "../components/very-funni-easter-egg/JorseSpawnerButton";

const FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME = "faq-accordion";
---

<div class="px-4 sm:px-12 md:px-24 lg:px-48 flex flex-col gap-4">
    <span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">FAQ</h2>
    </span>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">What is this?</p>
            <Fragment slot="content"
                >A website made to display an estimate of comments like "mod
                name?" from my channel.</Fragment
            >
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">Who is "TuxeBro?"</p>
            <Fragment slot="content"
                >Me, a sentient rock who makes Minecraft Create Mod videos,
                thats all.</Fragment
            >
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">"What is the 'mod name?' joke?"</p>
            <Fragment slot="content"
                >Basically a running joke made by my viewers, sarcastically not
                knowing the mod despite the names of the mod are already added
                into my description and title.
            </Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">"Was the 'mod name?' joke that bad?"</p>
            <Fragment slot="content">
                <div>
                    As TuxeBro, it's a <i>meh</i> joke. Similar how DougDoug felt
                    about "BALD" jokes. Or either Yahiamice and his fans' five hundred
                    "<JorseSpawnerButton client:idle />" comments within every
                    comment section of his.
                </div>

                <div>
                    Not even that mad, just mildly annoyed. But I lowkey
                    appreciate how a dumb running joke settled a creator's
                    distinct personality or branding in a weird way. And yea, it
                    is what it is lol.
                </div>
            </Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">Are the numbers even accurate?</p>
            <Fragment slot="content">
                <div>
                    Nope. I ran a separate local program that uses the YouTube
                    API to scan every comment from every video I made, and track
                    the "velocity" and amount of comments with the words like
                    "mod name?" and stuff. After that, I update this site with
                    the said velocity and the amount of comments and the website
                    will do a rough estimate of how many comments are there.
                </div>

                <div>
                    And YouTube API does not actually get EVERY comment inside
                    my channel. It does not include comments that isn't from a
                    video (more specifically text/image posts) and especially
                    spam comments.
                </div>

                <div>
                    I will occasionally update the data whenever I upload a
                    video or whenever I feel like it.
                </div>
            </Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">
                "I want to unironically spam the joke by 500 times because I
                wanna see the counters go high! Can I?"
            </p>
            <Fragment slot="content">
                <div class="text-lg font-bold">NEVER DO THAT.</div>

                <div>
                    If you even attempt to spam my comment section like "mod
                    name?" because you want to see the numbers go big, <b
                        >high chance that you will get shadow banned by
                        YouTube's moderation and it won't increase the counter
                        AT ALL</b
                    >.
                </div>

                <div>
                    I may let some comments like "mod name?" slide but please do
                    not even try to beat a decimated h*rse.
                </div>
            </Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">"Mod name?"</p>
            <Fragment slot="content">
                <Picture
                    src={thisCannotContinue}
                    formats={["webp", "avif", "jpg"]}
                    alt="bruh"
                />
            </Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">
                "No seriously, what are the typical mods you use in your
                videos?"
            </p>
            <Fragment slot="content"
                >Stay tuned for "mod name?" 2, I will update this website with
                the list of mods that I use.</Fragment
            >
        </AccordionItem>
        <AccordionItem groupName={FAQ_ACCORDION_GROUP_NAME}>
            <p slot="title">"WHEN IS MOD NAME 2????????"</p>
            <Fragment slot="content">soon</Fragment>
        </AccordionItem>
    </div>
</div>
